167
00:15:33,965 --> 00:15:36,990
Your assignment has four questions. One:

168
00:15:37,010 --> 00:15:42,166
a customer wants 99.8 percent trim success at 90 percent confidence.

169
00:15:42,186 --> 00:15:48,104
How many trims, and how many minutes, with zero failures and with one allowed,

170
00:15:48,124 --> 00:15:51,225
and over which conditions should they go?

171
00:15:51,625 --> 00:15:59,205
Two: a change may raise the trim failure rate at 4750 r/min to 1.2 percent.

172
00:15:59,225 --> 00:16:06,804
To be 99 percent sure of catching it each night, how many trims are needed,

173
00:16:06,824 --> 00:16:11,263
and what if they run at 4000 instead? Three:

174
00:16:11,283 --> 00:16:15,316
two candidate builds each stop 50 times.

175
00:16:15,336 --> 00:16:20,281
Find the one-sided Cpk and judge it against 1.33.

176
00:16:20,681 --> 00:16:26,398
Four: write 4 acceptance requirements for the overlock prototype,

177
00:16:26,418 --> 00:16:31,341
say at which level and with which case each is verified,

178
00:16:31,361 --> 00:16:36,901
and give a 240-minute nightly HIL allocation with your reasons.

179
00:16:37,301 --> 00:16:41,123
Submit the report on the WenQuest platform.

180
00:16:42,643 --> 00:16:46,645
There's also a ten-question quiz. For example,

181
00:16:46,665 --> 00:16:53,640
to show at least 99 percent success at 95 percent confidence with zero failures,

182
00:16:53,660 --> 00:16:56,088
how many trials do you need?

183
00:16:56,488 --> 00:16:56,768
Or,

184
00:16:56,788 --> 00:17:03,668
50 stops on HIL give a mean stop error of 0.40 degrees and a standard

185
00:17:03,688 --> 00:17:05,468
deviation of 0.12,

186
00:17:05,488 --> 00:17:10,268
with a 1 degree limit. What's the one-sided Cpk?

187
00:17:10,668 --> 00:17:15,837
You get three attempts, and the explanations appear as soon as you submit.

188
00:17:17,357 --> 00:17:19,059
Three things to remember.

189
00:17:19,459 --> 00:17:26,589
One: the test pyramid, unit, SIL, HIL, full machine and end-of-line,

190
00:17:26,609 --> 00:17:31,951
and catch each defect at the lowest layer that can.

191
00:17:32,351 --> 00:17:35,826
Two: statistics decides how many trials:

192
00:17:35,846 --> 00:17:40,457
zero-failure n is at least ln of 1 minus C over ln R;

193
00:17:40,477 --> 00:17:45,350
with failures use the lower bound; to catch regressions,

194
00:17:45,370 --> 00:17:49,369
spend trials on the most sensitive conditions.

195
00:17:49,769 --> 00:17:55,986
Three: continuous integration tests every commit, every night and every week,

196
00:17:56,006 --> 00:17:59,389
and every maturity stage exits on numbers.

